// LPDDR4 PHY on the DFI 1:4 interface for Lattice Nexus devices (CertusPro-NX, CrossLink-NX,
// Certus-NX, MachXO5-NX), built from the I/O logic's x4 gearing and the DQS buffers.
//
// It has the DFI interface of DfiLpddr4BehavPhy (see dfi.md next to this file) and drives the
// LPDDR4 pins of one x16 channel through the device's DDR blocks, which a build for a Nexus
// device takes from the primitive library (simulation models in skalp/primitives/nexus):
//   - clocks: the edge clock eclk (CK rate, from a PLL) through one ECLKSYNC (cascaded to the
//     command bank), an ECLKDIV /4 makes the DFI clock (SCLK), a DDRDLL measures the edge clock
//     for the DQS buffers;
//   - command: CK, CK_c, CA[5:0], CS and CKE through ODDRX4 (CA, CS and CKE then a DELAYB of CA_DELAY
//     steps); RESET_N is a fabric register;
//   - per byte lane: a DQSBUF; DQS through ODDRX4DQS and TSHX4DQS on DQSW; DQ and DMI through
//     ODDRX4DQ and TSHX4DQ on DQSW270; each DQ in through a DELAYA (DQ_IN_DELAY steps) into an
//     IDDRX4DQ on DQSR90 and the DQS buffer's FIFO pointers.
//
// Pins: the PHY ends at the I/O logic. Each bidirectional pin has an output (`*_o`), a tristate
// control (`*_t`, 1 = not driven) and the pad's input (`*_i`); the design's top level connects
// them to its pads (on Nexus: a BB per pin, with the LPDDR4 I/O standards). CK and DQS are
// pseudo-differential: the complement pins (`ck_c`, `dqs_c_*`) are single-ended outputs with their
// own gearing and the inverted data, as a differential output pad of these devices does not drive
// its complement pin (seen on a CertusPro-NX: CK_c and DQS_c stayed low, so the DRAM never took a
// command). Reads take the strobe from DQS_t alone. A simulation connects them to an
// LPDDR4 model, with the pad's value as the input (the PHY reads its own DQS back while it
// drives it, which write leveling uses).
//
// Timing at the pins: every DFI phase is one CK slot; a DFI cycle's four slots reach the pins
// together, a fixed number of DFI cycles after the controller drives them, commands and data
// alike. CK rises in the middle of each slot; CA, CS and CKE change at slot starts. Write data:
// a slot with dfi_wrdata_en is sent in the next slot at the pins; DQS rises at that slot's start
// plus the lane's write leveling delay and falls half a tCK later, with a 2 tCK static preamble
// and a 1 tCK postamble (driven low); DQ is centred on DQS (DQSW270 is three quarters of a tCK
// after DQSW, plus the lane's write DQ delay) and holds its last beat one more slot; DQ's drivers
// turn on a slot before the first data slot (inside the DQS preamble), as on a CertusPro-NX the
// first beat of a write that follows no other write otherwise reached the DRAM undriven (its ODT
// pulled it low: lone writes stored beat 0 with ones cleared). So, as with
// the behavioural PHY, a controller sets TPHY_WRLAT_ADJ = 3.
//
// Reads: each lane's read gate (the DQS buffer's READ) follows dfi_rddata_en, delayed by the
// lane's trained gate setting in eighths of a tCK (whole slots, then RDCLKSEL in 45 degree steps).
// The DQS buffer samples DQ on DQSR90 (DQS delayed a quarter tCK, moved by the lane's read
// delay) into the I/O logic FIFO and returns a DATAVALID word per eight beats, counted from the
// first strobe pulse its gate passed (as the device does): a BL16 read brings two, the half
// bursts in order. On a CertusPro-NX DATAVALID marks a lone burst's words, but in a run of
// back-to-back bursts it was seen to run a burst ahead of the words and later fall back, so a
// PHY that paired words by it shifted whole bursts and lost responses. So DATAVALID is used only
// by the gate training, which pairs words by it; the read eye training first measures the read
// return latency (from a half burst's end in dfi_rddata_en to the DFI cycle its word comes out
// of the gearing) on a lone burst, from the cycles whose words are the Read DQ Calibration
// pattern's halves, and from then on each half's word is taken at that latency.
// The words and the check of a training half are a register stage each. Once
// both lanes have a half burst it goes back on dfi_rddata_wN (four words, beats 2N and 2N+1 of
// both lanes, the earlier beat in [15:0]) with dfi_rddata_valid_wN. A controller
// keeps TRDDATA_EN_ADJ = 3; the gate training finds the burst after it.
// The DQS buffer also sees the PHY's own write strobes on its input. On a CertusPro-NX, with its
// gate shut, it still took part of a write's strobe into its read FIFO (one DATAVALID word
// after each write instead of two), which left the next read's beats a strobe pulse out of
// place in the words (the read after it came back right). So the gate is also opened around
// every write strobe, as for a write leveling strobe: the buffer then takes the write as a whole
// burst and stays in step; the words are never taken.
//
// Reset (as the device's LPDDR4 interface wants it): sync_clk, a free-running clock, runs the DDR
// reset sequence once the PLL locks: DLL reset and lock, DLL frozen, edge clocks stopped, the DQS
// buffers (with their state counters), the divider and every gearbox reset and released, edge
// clocks restarted, DLL released, and the DLL code taken by the DQS buffers with their clocks
// paused. The DDR reset changes only while the edge clocks are stopped: paths from it to the
// blocks it resets are false paths. Controller updates take the DLL code again (see below), so
// a controller sets CTRLUPD_CYC >= 8.
//
// Delay settings move in 12.5 ps steps, one step per two DFI cycles, without PAUSE: the DQS
// buffer's PAUSE stops its read side, so it is held only for a few cycles after a gate setting
// changes (and around DLL code updates); a long move (back from a failed write leveling sweep)
// would otherwise keep the gate shut through the next phase. At init the PHY resets the DLL,
// waits for it to lock, resets the DQS buffers and loads every setting (read and write delays in
// the middle) before raising dfi_init_complete. Each training sweep first moves its delay to where it starts (the read
// delay to the middle for the gate, to EYE_HALF below it for the read eye; the write delay to
// WDQ_HALF below the middle); an event sent while a delay moves is not evaluated.
//
// Training (PHY evaluation, as the behavioural PHY; each training event is evaluated over the
// TRAIN_WIN DFI cycles after its frame is sent, then the delays move, so the controller spaces
// events by TRAIN_GAP_CYC and WL_GAP_CYC >= 32):
//   write leveling (dfi_wrlvl_en): each dfi_wrlvl_strobe sends a DQS preamble and four pulses
//         (the DQS buffer returns no word for fewer) on both lanes with the lane's leveling
//         delay, and opens the read gate around them, so the DQS buffer samples DQ (the DRAM's
//         feedback from the previous strobe: any bit set at the first pulse means CK was high)
//         on the PHY's own DQS. The delay starts at 0 (DQS rising half a tCK before
//         CK) and moves up WL_STEP steps per strobe; each lane keeps the first delay whose
//         feedback goes from 0 to 1, moves back to it and raises its dfi_wrlvl_resp bit
//         (wrlvl_fail when WL_MAX steps pass without one). The edge comes about half a tCK
//         in, so WL_MAX (248 steps, 3.1 ns; at most 255 - WL_STEP, the delay being 8 bits) reaches
//         it down to 400 Mbps (half a tCK 2.5 ns) with board skew to spare.
//   read gate (dfi_rdlvl_gate_en): Read DQ Calibration bursts, the n-th with gate setting n
//         (0 to 8 x GATE_SLOTS - 1, from the slot of dfi_rddata_en), sampled with the read delay
//         in the middle; a setting passes when both half bursts come back as the Read DQ
//         Calibration pattern, which needs the gate to open in the preamble (opened later it
//         misses pulses and returns one word). The longest passing run ends where the gate would open
//         after the first DQS rise; each lane takes the middle of the run but no more than a tCK
//         before its end, inside the 2 tCK preamble (gate_fail if no run of 4).
//   read eye (dfi_rdlvl_en): the first burst whose words are the pattern's two halves, with
//         the read delay where the gate training left it, sets the read return latency (see
//         Reads); then
//         each burst is captured with the next read delay (EYE_STEP steps
//         apart, from EYE_HALF below the middle to EYE_HALF above) and compared with the Read DQ
//         Calibration pattern (RDC_PATTERN = {MR40, MR32}, per-lane inversion RDC_INV0/1 = MR15,
//         MR20); the lane takes the middle of the longest passing run (lvl_fail if none).
//   write DQ (dfi_wdqlvl_en): the PHY sends its own data on every write (byte k of a lane-0 burst
//         is {k, k}, inverted on odd beats; lane 1 is the inverse) and compares each read-back
//         with it; the write delay sweeps as the read delay does (WDQ_STEP, WDQ_HALF), and each
//         lane takes the middle of the longest passing run (wdq_fail if none).
// No read data comes back on DFI while any training enable is set.
//
// PHY updates: the PHY acknowledges controller updates and does not request any.

// write DQ training data: byte k of a lane-0 burst is {k, k}, inverted on odd beats
fn nx_wdq_byte(k: bit[4]) -> bit[8] {
    return if k[0] == 1 { ~{k, k} } else { {k, k} }
}

// word i of a write DQ training burst: beats 2i and 2i+1 of both lanes, the earlier in [15:0]
fn nx_wdq_word(i: bit[3]) -> bit[32] {
    let b0: bit[8] = nx_wdq_byte({i, 1'b0})
    let b1: bit[8] = nx_wdq_byte({i, 1'b1})
    return {~b1, b1, ~b0, b0}
}

// a lane-0 write DQ training burst, beat k in [8k+7:8k]
fn nx_wdq_lane(z: bit) -> bit[128] {
    return {nx_wdq_byte(4'd15), nx_wdq_byte(4'd14), nx_wdq_byte(4'd13), nx_wdq_byte(4'd12),
            nx_wdq_byte(4'd11), nx_wdq_byte(4'd10), nx_wdq_byte(4'd9), nx_wdq_byte(4'd8),
            nx_wdq_byte(4'd7), nx_wdq_byte(4'd6), nx_wdq_byte(4'd5), nx_wdq_byte(4'd4),
            nx_wdq_byte(4'd3), nx_wdq_byte(4'd2), nx_wdq_byte(4'd1), nx_wdq_byte(4'd0)}
}

// a Read DQ Calibration burst on one lane: beat k is all ones or all zeros per pattern bit k,
// inverted by the lane's mask
fn nx_rdc_lane(pat: bit[16], inv: bit[8]) -> bit[128] {
    return {
        if pat[15] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[14] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[13] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[12] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[11] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[10] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[9] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[8] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[7] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[6] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[5] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[4] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[3] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[2] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv },
        if pat[1] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }, if pat[0] == 1 { ~inv } else { inv }
    }
}

// One DQ pin: x4 output and tristate gearing on DQSW270, delayed input into x4 input gearing on
// DQSR90. d: D0..D7 (D0 first); t: one tristate bit per edge clock cycle (1 = not driven);
// q: Q0..Q7 (Q0 = the first beat).
pub entity NexusLpddr4DqPin<const IN_DELAY: nat = 0> {
    in eclk: clock
    in sclk: clock
    in dqsw270: clock
    in dqsr90: clock
    in rst: bit
    in load_n: bit
    in d: bit[8]
    in t: bit[4]
    in rdp: bit[3]
    in wrp: bit[3]
    out o: bit
    out ot: bit
    in i: bit
    out q: bit[8]
}

impl NexusLpddr4DqPin {
    inst od = ODDRX4DQ {
        D0: d[0], D1: d[1], D2: d[2], D3: d[3], D4: d[4], D5: d[5], D6: d[6], D7: d[7],
        DQSW270: dqsw270, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: rst
    }
    inst ts = TSHX4DQ {
        T0: t[0], T1: t[1], T2: t[2], T3: t[3],
        DQSW270: dqsw270, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: rst
    }
    inst dl = DELAYA<IN_DELAY> {
        A: i, LOAD_N: load_n, MOVE: 0, DIRECTION: 0, COARSE0: 0, COARSE1: 0,
        RANKSELECT: 0, RANKENABLE: 0, RANK0UPDATE: 0, RANK1UPDATE: 0
    }
    inst id = IDDRX4DQ {
        D: dl.Z, DQSR90: dqsr90, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: rst,
        RDPNTR0: rdp[0], RDPNTR1: rdp[1], RDPNTR2: rdp[2],
        WRPNTR0: wrp[0], WRPNTR1: wrp[1], WRPNTR2: wrp[2]
    }
    o = od.Q
    ot = ts.Q
    q = {id.Q7, id.Q6, id.Q5, id.Q4, id.Q3, id.Q2, id.Q1, id.Q0}
}

// One byte lane: the DQS buffer, DQS, 8 DQ and DMI (output only: data mask and DBI are off),
// and the lane's training.
//
// Inputs per DFI cycle, for the frame being sent: dq_d (pin b's D0..D7 in [8b+7:8b]), dq_tt and
// dqs_tt (one tristate bit per slot), dqs_d; rd_win: dfi_rddata_en of the last 12 slots, the
// newest (captured) frame in [11:8], the frame being sent in [7:4]; wl_frame: the frame carries a write leveling pulse; wr_gate:
// the read gate's slots around the frame's write strobe pulses; tr_start: a
// training event (strobe or read burst) is in the frame being sent.
pub entity NexusLpddr4Lane<
    const IN_DELAY: nat = 0,
    const GATE_SLOTS: nat = 8,
    const TRAIN_WIN: nat = 14,
    const WL_STEP: nat = 4,
    const WL_MAX: nat = 248,
    const EYE_STEP: nat = 4,
    const EYE_HALF: nat = 64,
    const WDQ_STEP: nat = 4,
    const WDQ_HALF: nat = 64
> {
    in eclk: clock
    in sclk: clock
    // rst: the lane's fabric logic; io_rst: the DDR reset of its DQS buffer and I/O logic
    // (with the edge clock stopped, see the PHY); io_pause: the PHY's PAUSE around DLL code updates
    in rst: bit
    in io_rst: bit
    in io_pause: bit
    in load: bit
    in dllcode: bit[9]
    in dq_d: bit[64]
    in dq_tt: bit[4]
    in dqs_d: bit[8]
    in dqs_tt: bit[4]
    in rd_win: bit[12]
    in wl_frame: bit[3]
    in wr_gate: bit[4]
    in tr_start: bit
    in wl_en: bit
    in gate_en: bit
    in eye_en: bit
    in wdq_en: bit
    in exp_rdc: bit[128]
    in exp_wdq: bit[128]
    // pins
    out dq_o: bit[8]
    out dq_t: bit[8]
    in dq_i: bit[8]
    out dmi_o: bit
    out dmi_t: bit
    out dqs_o: bit
    out dqs_t: bit
    in dqs_i: bit
    // the complement strobe pin: the inverted strobe, driven when DQS is
    out dqs_c_o: bit
    out dqs_c_t: bit
    // read data: eight beats (beat k in [8k+7:8k]) of a burst, outside training
    out dv: bit
    out half: bit[64]
    // training
    out busy: bit
    out resp_wl: bit
    out resp_gate: bit
    out resp_eye: bit
    out resp_wdq: bit
    out wl_fail: bit
    out gate_fail: bit
    out eye_fail: bit
    out wdq_fail: bit
    out wl_pos: bit[8]
    out gate_set: bit[8]
    out rd_pos: bit[8]
    out wr_pos: bit[8]
    out sweep_map: bit[64]
    // the read latency the read eye step measured, in slots
    out rd_lat_o: bit[8]
    out bursts: bit[16]
}

impl NexusLpddr4Lane {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------ delay settings
    // positions as the DQS buffer holds them (read and write: 128 = the middle)
    signal rdp_r: bit[8] = 128
    signal wrp_r: bit[8] = 128
    signal wlp_r: bit[8] = 0
    // steps still to move, the direction (1 = down) and the MOVE outputs
    signal rd_n: bit[8] = 0
    signal wr_n: bit[8] = 0
    signal wl_n: bit[8] = 0
    signal rd_dn: bit = 0
    signal wr_dn: bit = 0
    signal wl_dn: bit = 0
    signal rd_mv: bit = 0
    signal wr_mv: bit = 0
    signal wl_mv: bit = 0
    let moving: bit = if rd_n != 0 || wr_n != 0 || wl_n != 0 || rd_mv == 1 || wr_mv == 1 || wl_mv == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    // after a gate setting changes, the DQS buffer pauses a few cycles
    signal pause_n: bit[3] = 0
    let pause: bit = if pause_n != 0 { 1 } else { 0 }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ training state
    signal gsel: bit[8] = 0
    signal win: bit[8] = 0
    // the event started with every delay settled and the gate not paused: an event sent while a
    // delay still moves (to the start of a sweep) is not evaluated, the controller sends another
    signal ev_ok: bit = 0
    signal nv: bit[2] = 0
    signal mism: bit = 0
    signal fb: bit = 0
    // sweep: setting index or position of the event being evaluated, run and best run
    signal idx: bit[8] = 0
    signal run_st: bit[8] = 0
    // the last sweep's results, one bit per evaluated position (the latest in bit 0)
    signal sw_map: bit[64] = 0
    signal run_ln: bit[8] = 0
    signal best_st: bit[8] = 0
    signal best_end: bit[8] = 0
    signal best_ln: bit[8] = 0
    // write leveling: events seen, position of the last strobe, last feedback
    signal wl_k: bit[8] = 0
    signal wl_last: bit[8] = 0
    signal wl_fb_p: bit = 0
    signal wl_best: bit[8] = 0
    // a phase's sweep is over; its result is being moved to
    signal fin: bit = 0
    signal r_wl: bit = 0
    signal r_gate: bit = 0
    signal r_eye: bit = 0
    signal r_wdq: bit = 0
    signal f_wl: bit = 0
    signal f_gate: bit = 0
    signal f_eye: bit = 0
    signal f_wdq: bit = 0
    signal wl_q: bit = 0
    signal gate_q: bit = 0
    signal eye_q: bit = 0
    signal wdq_q: bit = 0
    signal nburst: bit[16] = 0
    signal load_q: bit = 0

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ read return latency
    // Where each half burst ends, from the read enables: rd_win's newest cycle (slots 8-11) is
    // followed slot by slot, counting enabled slots in a run (mod 4) and which half the next end
    // is; a run's half ends are its 4th, 8th, ... enabled slots
    signal run_c: bit[2] = 0
    signal run_h: bit = 0
    // half ends of the 16 cycles before this one, by age in slots (bit 0: 4 slots old)
    signal mh: bit[64] = 0
    // age in slots of the last first-half end (saturating), the trained latency in slots from a
    // half's end to the cycle its word is taken in, and whether it holds / is being measured
    signal age0: bit[8] = 255
    signal rd_lat: bit[8] = 0
    signal have_lat: bit = 0
    signal meas: bit = 0
    // a first-half word was seen in the last cycle while measuring, and its latency
    signal lat_p: bit = 0
    signal lat_c: bit[8] = 0

    let training: bit = if wl_en == 1 || gate_en == 1 || eye_en == 1 || wdq_en == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let gate_n: bit[8] = GATE_SLOTS * 8
    let train_win: bit[8] = TRAIN_WIN
    let wl_step: bit[8] = WL_STEP
    let wl_max: bit[8] = WL_MAX
    let eye_step: bit[8] = EYE_STEP
    let eye_top: bit[8] = 128 + EYE_HALF
    let eye_bot: bit[8] = 128 - EYE_HALF
    let wdq_step: bit[8] = WDQ_STEP
    let wdq_top: bit[8] = 128 + WDQ_HALF
    let wdq_bot: bit[8] = 128 - WDQ_HALF

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ read gate
    let gs: bit[4] = {1'b0, gsel[5:3]}
    let ri0: bit[4] = 8 - gs
    let ri1: bit[4] = 9 - gs
    let ri2: bit[4] = 10 - gs
    let ri3: bit[4] = 11 - gs
    // a write leveling strobe: the gate opens in the last preamble slot and stays open two slots
    // past the four pulses, which the leveling delay moves later
    let read_n: bit[4] = if wl_frame[0] == 1 { 4'b1000 } else {
        if wl_frame[1] == 1 { 4'b1111 } else {
            if wl_frame[2] == 1 { 4'b0011 } else { {rd_win[ri3], rd_win[ri2], rd_win[ri1], rd_win[ri0]} | wr_gate }
        }
    }
    let sel_n: bit[4] = if wl_en == 1 { 4'b0000 } else { {1'b0, gsel[2:0]} }

    // the half ends among this cycle's slots (slot 0 first), each with the half it ends
    let e0: bit = rd_win[8]
    let e1: bit = rd_win[9]
    let e2: bit = rd_win[10]
    let e3: bit = rd_win[11]
    let k0: bit[2] = run_c
    let h0: bit = run_h
    let m0: bit = if e0 == 1 && k0 == 3 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let k1: bit[2] = if e0 == 1 { k0 + 1 } else { 0 }
    let h1: bit = if e0 == 0 { 0 } else { if m0 == 1 { ~h0 } else { h0 } }
    let m1: bit = if e1 == 1 && k1 == 3 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let k2: bit[2] = if e1 == 1 { k1 + 1 } else { 0 }
    let h2: bit = if e1 == 0 { 0 } else { if m1 == 1 { ~h1 } else { h1 } }
    let m2: bit = if e2 == 1 && k2 == 3 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let k3: bit[2] = if e2 == 1 { k2 + 1 } else { 0 }
    let h3: bit = if e2 == 0 { 0 } else { if m2 == 1 { ~h2 } else { h2 } }
    let m3: bit = if e3 == 1 && k3 == 3 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let k4: bit[2] = if e3 == 1 { k3 + 1 } else { 0 }
    let h4: bit = if e3 == 0 { 0 } else { if m3 == 1 { ~h3 } else { h3 } }
    // first-half ends (a read's first word)
    let z0: bit = if m0 == 1 && h0 == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let z1: bit = if m1 == 1 && h1 == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let z2: bit = if m2 == 1 && h2 == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let z3: bit = if m3 == 1 && h3 == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    // every half end by age in slots: 0 is this cycle's slot 3
    let hist: bit[68] = {mh, m0, m1, m2, m3}
    let age0_n: bit[8] = if z3 == 1 { 0 } else { if z2 == 1 { 1 } else { if z1 == 1 { 2 } else {
        if z0 == 1 { 3 } else { if age0 > 251 { 255 } else { age0 + 4 } } } } }
    // a half's word is taken in the cycle its end, rd_lat slots on, falls in
    let lat_win: bit[68] = hist >> rd_lat
    let take: bit = if lat_win[3:0] != 0 { 1 } else { 0 }

    inst dqs = DQSBUF {
        DQSI: dqs_i, ECLKIN: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst,
        PAUSE: pause | io_pause,
        RSTSMCNT: io_rst, RDCLKSEL: sel_n, READ: read_n,
        RDDIR: rd_dn, RDLOADN: ~load, READMOVE: rd_mv, SELCLK: 0,
        WRDIR: wr_dn, WRLOAD_N: ~load, WRMOVE: wr_mv,
        WRLVDIR: wl_dn, WRLVLOAD_N: ~load, WRLVMOVE: wl_mv,
        DLLCODE: dllcode
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ DQS and the pins
    inst dqs_od = ODDRX4DQS {
        D0: dqs_d[0], D1: dqs_d[1], D2: dqs_d[2], D3: dqs_d[3],
        D4: dqs_d[4], D5: dqs_d[5], D6: dqs_d[6], D7: dqs_d[7],
        DQSW: dqs.DQSW, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst
    }
    inst dqs_ts = TSHX4DQS {
        T0: dqs_tt[0], T1: dqs_tt[1], T2: dqs_tt[2], T3: dqs_tt[3],
        DQSW: dqs.DQSW, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst
    }
    signal dqs_n: bit[8]
    dqs_n = ~dqs_d
    inst dqsc_od = ODDRX4DQS {
        D0: dqs_n[0], D1: dqs_n[1], D2: dqs_n[2], D3: dqs_n[3],
        D4: dqs_n[4], D5: dqs_n[5], D6: dqs_n[6], D7: dqs_n[7],
        DQSW: dqs.DQSW, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst
    }
    inst dqsc_ts = TSHX4DQS {
        T0: dqs_tt[0], T1: dqs_tt[1], T2: dqs_tt[2], T3: dqs_tt[3],
        DQSW: dqs.DQSW, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst
    }
    signal w270: clock
    signal r90: clock
    w270 = dqs.DQSW270
    r90 = dqs.DQSR90
    inst p0 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[7:0], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[0]
    }
    inst p1 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[15:8], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[1]
    }
    inst p2 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[23:16], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[2]
    }
    inst p3 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[31:24], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[3]
    }
    inst p4 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[39:32], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[4]
    }
    inst p5 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[47:40], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[5]
    }
    inst p6 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[55:48], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[6]
    }
    inst p7 = NexusLpddr4DqPin<IN_DELAY> {
        eclk: eclk, sclk: sclk, dqsw270: w270, dqsr90: r90, rst: io_rst, load_n: ~load,
        d: dq_d[63:56], t: dq_tt, rdp: dqs.RDPNTR, wrp: dqs.WRPNTR, i: dq_i[7]
    }
    inst dmi_od = ODDRX4DQ {
        D0: 0, D1: 0, D2: 0, D3: 0, D4: 0, D5: 0, D6: 0, D7: 0,
        DQSW270: w270, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst
    }
    inst dmi_ts = TSHX4DQ {
        T0: dq_tt[0], T1: dq_tt[1], T2: dq_tt[2], T3: dq_tt[3],
        DQSW270: w270, ECLK: eclk, SCLK: sclk, RST: io_rst
    }

    // eight beats of the lane, beat k in [8k+7:8k]
    let qb0: bit[8] = p0.q
    let qb1: bit[8] = p1.q
    let qb2: bit[8] = p2.q
    let qb3: bit[8] = p3.q
    let qb4: bit[8] = p4.q
    let qb5: bit[8] = p5.q
    let qb6: bit[8] = p6.q
    let qb7: bit[8] = p7.q
    let hb: bit[64] = {
        qb7[7], qb6[7], qb5[7], qb4[7], qb3[7], qb2[7], qb1[7], qb0[7],
        qb7[6], qb6[6], qb5[6], qb4[6], qb3[6], qb2[6], qb1[6], qb0[6],
        qb7[5], qb6[5], qb5[5], qb4[5], qb3[5], qb2[5], qb1[5], qb0[5],
        qb7[4], qb6[4], qb5[4], qb4[4], qb3[4], qb2[4], qb1[4], qb0[4],
        qb7[3], qb6[3], qb5[3], qb4[3], qb3[3], qb2[3], qb1[3], qb0[3],
        qb7[2], qb6[2], qb5[2], qb4[2], qb3[2], qb2[2], qb1[2], qb0[2],
        qb7[1], qb6[1], qb5[1], qb4[1], qb3[1], qb2[1], qb1[1], qb0[1],
        qb7[0], qb6[0], qb5[0], qb4[0], qb3[0], qb2[0], qb1[0], qb0[0]
    }
    // The gearbox words, their DATAVALID and BURSTDETECT, registered beside the fabric before
    // anything else uses them: the I/O logic is at the die edge, a routing hop of its own
    signal hb_r: bit[64] = 0
    signal dv_r: bit = 0

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ half bursts
    // Each DATAVALID word holds eight beats counted from the first strobe pulse the gate passed:
    // a half burst, the two of a BL16 read in order. On the device DATAVALID marks the words of
    // a lone burst, but in a run of back-to-back bursts it can move a burst ahead of the words
    // and back again, so once the read return latency is trained (at the start of the read eye
    // training, from a lone burst's words) each half's word is taken at that latency
    // from the half's end in the read enables; the gate training (whose setting the latency
    // depends on) uses DATAVALID
    let lat_on: bit = if have_lat == 1 && gate_en == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let hv: bit = if wl_en == 1 { 0 } else { if lat_on == 1 { take } else { dv_r } }
    // The latency is measured on a lone read DQ calibration burst with the delays settled, from
    // its data rather than its DATAVALID (on the device DATAVALID can rise a cycle before the
    // burst's first word): the cycle whose word is the pattern's first half, followed by a cycle
    // whose word is its second half. That burst's first half ended age0_n slots before the first
    // of the two cycles, and a latency of 0 to 3 slots less takes its word in that cycle; the
    // middle of that range is kept (64 slots at most, the history's reach)
    let lat_h0: bit = if meas == 1 && moving == 0 && pause == 0 && age0_n <= 66 && hb_r == exp_rdc[63:0] { 1 } else { 0 }
    let lat_meas: bit = if lat_p == 1 && hb_r == exp_rdc[127:64] { 1 } else { 0 }
    let lat_n: bit[8] = if age0_n >= 2 { age0_n - 2 } else { 0 }
    let hh: bit[64] = hb_r
    // each half burst, registered: it leaves the PHY and is checked during training from here
    signal hv_r: bit = 0
    signal hh_r: bit[64] = 0

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ evaluation of an event
    let in_win: bit = if win != 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let last_win: bit = if win == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let exp_h: bit[64] = if wdq_en == 1 {
        if nv == 0 { exp_wdq[63:0] } else { exp_wdq[127:64] }
    } else {
        if nv == 0 { exp_rdc[63:0] } else { exp_rdc[127:64] }
    }
    // a half's check lands a cycle after the half (the comparison is a stage of its own)
    signal bad_q: bit = 0
    let h_bad: bit = if hv_r == 1 && (nv >= 2 || hh_r != exp_h) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let mism_n: bit = if mism == 1 || bad_q == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let nv_n: bit[2] = if hv_r == 1 && nv != 3 { nv + 1 } else { nv }
    let fb_n: bit = if fb == 1 || (dv_r == 1 && hb_r[15:0] != 0) { 1 } else { 0 }
    // the event's result: both halves came back, as expected (gate: the setting passes when
    // the gate opened in the preamble and so took the whole burst, two words, in order)
    let data_ok: bit = if nv_n == 2 && mism_n == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let pass: bit = data_ok
    // the sweep's position of the event (gate: its setting)
    let pos: bit[8] = if gate_en == 1 { gsel } else { if eye_en == 1 { rdp_r } else { wrp_r } }
    let rl: bit[8] = run_ln + 1
    let rs: bit[8] = if run_ln == 0 { pos } else { run_st }
    let better: bit = if pass == 1 && rl > best_ln { 1 } else { 0 }
    let bl_n: bit[8] = if better == 1 { rl } else { best_ln }
    let bs_n: bit[8] = if better == 1 { rs } else { best_st }
    let be_n: bit[8] = if better == 1 { pos } else { best_end }
    // the sweep's result, a cycle after its last event, from the best run it kept
    // (positions reach 192, so the sum takes 9 bits)
    let mid_s: bit[9] = {1'b0, best_st} + {1'b0, best_end}
    let mid: bit[8] = mid_s[8:1]
    // the gate: settings pass while it opens in the DQS preamble (or before DQS is driven), up
    // to the first rising edge; it goes to the middle of the passing run, but no more than a
    // tCK (8 settings) before that edge, so it stays inside the 2 tCK preamble
    let g_ok: bit = if best_ln >= 4 && best_end >= 7 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let g_floor: bit[8] = best_end - 7
    signal calc: bit = 0
    // the sweep ends with this event
    let gate_last: bit = if gsel + 1 >= gate_n { 1 } else { 0 }
    let eye_last: bit = if rdp_r + eye_step > eye_top { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wdq_last: bit = if wrp_r + wdq_step > wdq_top { 1 } else { 0 }
    let sweeping: bit = if (gate_en == 1 && gate_q == 1 && r_gate == 0) || (eye_en == 1 && eye_q == 1 && r_eye == 0) || (wdq_en == 1 && wdq_q == 1 && r_wdq == 0) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let evaluate: bit = if last_win == 1 && ev_ok == 1 && sweeping == 1 && fin == 0 && calc == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    // write leveling: this strobe's sample is the feedback of the strobe before it
    let wl_sweep: bit = if wl_en == 1 && wl_q == 1 && r_wl == 0 && fin == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wl_eval: bit = if last_win == 1 && ev_ok == 1 && wl_sweep == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wl_hit: bit = if wl_k >= 2 && wl_fb_p == 0 && fb_n == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wl_end: bit = if wlp_r + wl_step > wl_max { 1 } else { 0 }
    let any_start: bit = if (wl_en == 1 && wl_q == 0) || (gate_en == 1 && gate_q == 0) || (eye_en == 1 && eye_q == 0) || (wdq_en == 1 && wdq_q == 0) { 1 } else { 0 }

    on(sclk.rise) {
        hb_r = hb
        dv_r = dqs.DATAVALID
        run_c = k4
        run_h = h4
        mh = hist[63:0]
        age0 = age0_n
        hv_r = hv
        hh_r = hh
        bad_q = h_bad
        if pause_n != 0 {
            pause_n = pause_n - 1
        }
        // ---------------------------------------------------------- moves
        if load == 1 {
            rdp_r = 128
            wrp_r = 128
            wlp_r = 0
            rd_n = 0
            wr_n = 0
            wl_n = 0
            rd_mv = 0
            wr_mv = 0
            wl_mv = 0
        } else {
            if rd_mv == 1 {
                rd_mv = 0
            } else if rd_n != 0 {
                rd_mv = 1
                rd_n = rd_n - 1
                rdp_r = if rd_dn == 1 { rdp_r - 1 } else { rdp_r + 1 }
            }
            if wr_mv == 1 {
                wr_mv = 0
            } else if wr_n != 0 {
                wr_mv = 1
                wr_n = wr_n - 1
                wrp_r = if wr_dn == 1 { wrp_r - 1 } else { wrp_r + 1 }
            }
            if wl_mv == 1 {
                wl_mv = 0
            } else if wl_n != 0 {
                wl_mv = 1
                wl_n = wl_n - 1
                wlp_r = if wl_dn == 1 { wlp_r - 1 } else { wlp_r + 1 }
            }
        }
        load_q = load

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- phases start
        wl_q = wl_en
        gate_q = gate_en
        eye_q = eye_en
        wdq_q = wdq_en
        if any_start == 1 {
            sw_map = 0
            run_ln = 0
            best_ln = 0
            best_st = 0
            best_end = 0
            fin = 0
            calc = 0
            win = 0
            wl_k = 0
            wl_fb_p = 0
        }
        if wl_en == 1 && wl_q == 0 {
            r_wl = 0
            f_wl = 0
        }
        // each sweep first moves its delay to where it starts: the gate's read delay to the
        // middle (the strobe's quarter cycle, so the training data is sampled in its eye), the
        // read eye's and the write DQ's to the bottom of their sweeps
        if gate_en == 1 && gate_q == 0 {
            r_gate = 0
            f_gate = 0
            gsel = 0
            have_lat = 0
            pause_n = 4
            rd_dn = if rdp_r > 128 { 1 } else { 0 }
            rd_n = if rdp_r > 128 { rdp_r - 128 } else { 128 - rdp_r }
        }
        // the read eye first measures the read return latency, with the read delay where the
        // gate training left it, and then moves to the bottom of its sweep
        if eye_en == 1 && eye_q == 0 {
            r_eye = 0
            f_eye = 0
            meas = 1
            have_lat = 0
        }
        lat_p = lat_h0
        lat_c = lat_n
        if lat_meas == 1 {
            meas = 0
            lat_p = 0
            have_lat = 1
            rd_lat = lat_c
            rd_dn = if rdp_r > eye_bot { 1 } else { 0 }
            rd_n = if rdp_r > eye_bot { rdp_r - eye_bot } else { eye_bot - rdp_r }
        }
        if wdq_en == 1 && wdq_q == 0 {
            r_wdq = 0
            f_wdq = 0
            wr_dn = if wrp_r > wdq_bot { 1 } else { 0 }
            wr_n = if wrp_r > wdq_bot { wrp_r - wdq_bot } else { wdq_bot - wrp_r }
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- an event's window
        if tr_start == 1 && training == 1 {
            win = train_win
            ev_ok = if moving == 0 && pause == 0 && meas == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
            nv = 0
            mism = 0
            fb = 0
        } else if in_win == 1 {
            win = win - 1
            nv = nv_n
            mism = mism_n
            fb = fb_n
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- gate, eye, write DQ sweeps
        if evaluate == 1 {
            sw_map = {sw_map[62:0], pass}
            if pass == 1 {
                run_st = rs
                run_ln = rl
            } else {
                run_ln = 0
            }
            best_ln = bl_n
            best_st = bs_n
            best_end = be_n
            if gate_en == 1 {
                if gate_last == 1 {
                    calc = 1
                } else {
                    gsel = gsel + 1
                }
                pause_n = 4
            }
            if eye_en == 1 {
                if eye_last == 1 {
                    calc = 1
                } else {
                    rd_dn = 0
                    rd_n = eye_step
                }
            }
            if wdq_en == 1 {
                if wdq_last == 1 {
                    calc = 1
                } else {
                    wr_dn = 0
                    wr_n = wdq_step
                }
            }
        }
        // the sweep's result, from the best run now held
        if calc == 1 {
            calc = 0
            fin = 1
            if gate_en == 1 {
                gsel = if g_ok == 0 { 0 } else { if mid > g_floor { mid } else { g_floor } }
                f_gate = if g_ok == 1 { 0 } else { 1 }
                pause_n = 4
            }
            if eye_en == 1 {
                f_eye = if best_ln == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
                rd_dn = 1
                rd_n = if best_ln == 0 { rdp_r - 128 } else { rdp_r - mid }
            }
            if wdq_en == 1 {
                f_wdq = if best_ln == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
                wr_dn = 1
                wr_n = if best_ln == 0 { wrp_r - 128 } else { wrp_r - mid }
            }
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- write leveling
        if wl_eval == 1 {
            wl_k = wl_k + 1
            if wl_k >= 1 {
                wl_fb_p = fb_n
            }
            if wl_hit == 1 {
                fin = 1
                wl_best = wl_last
                wl_dn = 1
                wl_n = wlp_r - wl_last
            } else if wl_end == 1 {
                fin = 1
                f_wl = 1
                wl_dn = 1
                wl_n = wlp_r
            } else {
                wl_last = wlp_r
                wl_dn = 0
                wl_n = wl_step
            }
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- results once moved
        if fin == 1 && moving == 0 && pause_n == 0 {
            if wl_en == 1 && r_wl == 0 {
                r_wl = 1
                fin = 0
            }
            if gate_en == 1 && r_gate == 0 {
                r_gate = 1
                fin = 0
            }
            if eye_en == 1 && r_eye == 0 {
                r_eye = 1
                fin = 0
            }
            if wdq_en == 1 && r_wdq == 0 {
                r_wdq = 1
                fin = 0
            }
        }
        if hv_r == 1 && training == 0 {
            nburst = nburst + 1
        }
    }

    // pins
    dq_o = {p7.o, p6.o, p5.o, p4.o, p3.o, p2.o, p1.o, p0.o}
    dq_t = {p7.ot, p6.ot, p5.ot, p4.ot, p3.ot, p2.ot, p1.ot, p0.ot}
    dmi_o = dmi_od.Q
    dmi_t = dmi_ts.Q
    dqs_o = dqs_od.Q
    dqs_t = dqs_ts.Q
    dqs_c_o = dqsc_od.Q
    dqs_c_t = dqsc_ts.Q

    dv = if hv_r == 1 && training == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    half = hh_r
    busy = moving
    resp_wl = if wl_en == 1 && r_wl == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    resp_gate = if gate_en == 1 && r_gate == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    resp_eye = if eye_en == 1 && r_eye == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    resp_wdq = if wdq_en == 1 && r_wdq == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    wl_fail = f_wl
    gate_fail = f_gate
    eye_fail = f_eye
    wdq_fail = f_wdq
    wl_pos = wlp_r
    gate_set = gsel
    rd_pos = rdp_r
    wr_pos = wrp_r
    sweep_map = sw_map
    rd_lat_o = rd_lat
    bursts = nburst
}

// The PHY: DFI 1:4 to one x16 LPDDR4 channel (see the top of this file).
pub entity DfiLpddr4NexusPhy<
    const RDC_PATTERN: nat = 15450,
    const RDC_INV0: nat = 0,
    const RDC_INV1: nat = 0,
    const CA_DELAY: nat = 0,
    const DQ_IN_DELAY: nat = 0,
    const GATE_SLOTS: nat = 8,
    const TRAIN_WIN: nat = 14,
    const WL_STEP: nat = 4,
    const WL_MAX: nat = 248,
    const EYE_STEP: nat = 4,
    const EYE_HALF: nat = 64,
    const WDQ_STEP: nat = 4,
    const WDQ_HALF: nat = 64
> {
    // the edge clock (CK rate) and its PLL's lock
    in eclk: clock
    in pll_lock: bit
    // a free-running clock of at most 200 MHz (such as the PLL's reference): the DDR reset
    // sequence runs on it while the edge clock, and so the DFI clock, is stopped
    in sync_clk: clock
    out dfi_clk: clock
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- DFI from the controller
    in dfi_cs_p0: bit
    in dfi_cs_p1: bit
    in dfi_cs_p2: bit
    in dfi_cs_p3: bit
    in dfi_address_p0: bit[6]
    in dfi_address_p1: bit[6]
    in dfi_address_p2: bit[6]
    in dfi_address_p3: bit[6]
    in dfi_cke_p0: bit
    in dfi_cke_p1: bit
    in dfi_cke_p2: bit
    in dfi_cke_p3: bit
    in dfi_reset_n_p0: bit
    in dfi_reset_n_p1: bit
    in dfi_reset_n_p2: bit
    in dfi_reset_n_p3: bit
    in dfi_wrdata_en_p0: bit
    in dfi_wrdata_en_p1: bit
    in dfi_wrdata_en_p2: bit
    in dfi_wrdata_en_p3: bit
    in dfi_wrdata_p0: bit[32]
    in dfi_wrdata_p1: bit[32]
    in dfi_wrdata_p2: bit[32]
    in dfi_wrdata_p3: bit[32]
    in dfi_wrdata_mask_p0: bit[4]
    in dfi_wrdata_mask_p1: bit[4]
    in dfi_wrdata_mask_p2: bit[4]
    in dfi_wrdata_mask_p3: bit[4]
    in dfi_rddata_en_p0: bit
    in dfi_rddata_en_p1: bit
    in dfi_rddata_en_p2: bit
    in dfi_rddata_en_p3: bit
    in dfi_init_start: bit
    in dfi_ctrlupd_req: bit
    in dfi_phyupd_ack: bit
    in dfi_rdlvl_gate_en: bit
    in dfi_rdlvl_en: bit
    in dfi_wrlvl_en: bit
    in dfi_wrlvl_strobe: bit
    in dfi_wdqlvl_en: bit
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- DFI to the controller
    out dfi_rddata_w0: bit[32]
    out dfi_rddata_w1: bit[32]
    out dfi_rddata_w2: bit[32]
    out dfi_rddata_w3: bit[32]
    out dfi_rddata_valid_w0: bit
    out dfi_rddata_valid_w1: bit
    out dfi_rddata_valid_w2: bit
    out dfi_rddata_valid_w3: bit
    out dfi_init_complete: bit
    out dfi_ctrlupd_ack: bit
    out dfi_phyupd_req: bit
    out dfi_rdlvl_gate_resp: bit[2]
    out dfi_rdlvl_resp: bit[2]
    out dfi_wrlvl_resp: bit[2]
    out dfi_wdqlvl_resp: bit[2]
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LPDDR4 pins (I/O logic side)
    out ck_t: bit
    out ck_c: bit
    out cke: bit
    out cs: bit
    out ca: bit[6]
    out reset_n: bit
    // per byte lane l: DQ[8l+7:8l], DQS[l], DMI[l]; *_t: 1 = not driven
    out dq_o: bit[16]
    out dq_t: bit[16]
    in dq_i: bit[16]
    out dqs_o: bit[2]
    out dqs_t: bit[2]
    in dqs_i: bit[2]
    // the complement strobe pins (outputs only: reads use DQS_t)
    out dqs_c_o: bit[2]
    out dqs_c_t: bit[2]
    out dmi_o: bit[2]
    out dmi_t: bit[2]
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- status
    // the DLL's lock flag, synchronized to SCLK
    out dll_lock: bit
    out gate_dly0: bit[8]
    out gate_dly1: bit[8]
    out rd_dly0: bit[8]
    out rd_dly1: bit[8]
    out wl_dly0: bit[8]
    out wl_dly1: bit[8]
    out wdq_dly0: bit[8]
    out wdq_dly1: bit[8]
    out gate_fail: bit[2]
    out lvl_fail: bit[2]
    out wrlvl_fail: bit[2]
    out wdq_fail: bit[2]
    // half bursts each lane has returned outside training
    out bursts0: bit[16]
    out bursts1: bit[16]
    // each lane's last training sweep (after training: the write DQ sweep), one bit per
    // evaluated position from the bottom up, the top in bit 0 (1 = passed)
    out sweep_map0: bit[64]
    out sweep_map1: bit[64]
    // each lane's read latency (slots from READ to its words), as the read eye step measured it
    out rd_lat0: bit[8]
    out rd_lat1: bit[8]
    out ctrlupd_count: bit[16]
}

impl DfiLpddr4NexusPhy {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------ clocks
    // One edge clock synchronizer for the data and the command pins: gearing needs its edge clock
    // and SCLK from the same synchronizer and divider, so a command bank beside the data bank
    // takes this edge clock through its cascade mux (as Lattice's own LPDDR4 interface does).
    inst es_dq = ECLKSYNC { ECLKIN: eclk, STOP: eclk_stop }
    signal eclk_ca: clock
    signal eclk_dq: clock
    eclk_dq = es_dq.ECLKOUT
    eclk_ca = eclk_dq
    inst ediv = ECLKDIV<4> { ECLKIN: eclk_dq, DIVRST: ddr_rst, SLIP: 0 }
    signal sclk: clock
    sclk = ediv.DIVOUT
    inst dll = DDRDLL { CLKIN: eclk_dq, RST: dll_rst, FREEZE: dll_freeze, UDDCNTL_N: dll_udd_n }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ DDR reset sequence (sync_clk)
    // As the device's LPDDR4 interface wants it (FPGA-IPUG-02154): once the PLL and the DLL
    // lock, freeze the DLL, stop the edge clocks, pulse the DDR reset (the DQS buffers with
    // their state counters, the divider and every gearbox), restart the edge clocks (SCLK
    // then starts in step with them), release the DLL, and update the DQS buffers' delay code
    // with their clocks paused. Then the DFI side (SCLK) loads the delay settings.
    // ss: 0 wait for the PLL, 1 DLL reset, 2 wait for the DLL, 3 frozen, 4 stopped, 5 DDR
    // reset, 6 reset released (still stopped), 7 restarted, 8 unfrozen, 9 code update, 10 ready
    #[cdc]
    signal s_pll_m: bit = 0
    signal s_pll: bit = 0
    #[cdc]
    signal s_dll_m: bit = 0
    signal s_dll: bit = 0
    signal ss: bit[4] = 0
    signal scnt: bit[5] = 0
    signal dll_rst: bit = 1
    signal dll_freeze: bit = 0
    signal eclk_stop: bit = 0
    signal ddr_rst: bit = 0
    signal init_pause: bit = 0
    signal init_udd_n: bit = 1
    signal io_ready: bit = 0
    on(sync_clk.rise) {
        s_pll_m = pll_lock
        s_pll = s_pll_m
        s_dll_m = dll.LOCK
        s_dll = s_dll_m
        scnt = scnt + 1
        if s_pll == 0 {
            // the PLL lost lock (or has not locked yet): start over
            ss = 0
            dll_rst = 1
            dll_freeze = 0
            eclk_stop = 0
            ddr_rst = 0
            init_pause = 0
            init_udd_n = 1
            io_ready = 0
        } else if ss == 0 {
            ss = 1
            scnt = 0
        } else if ss == 1 {
            if scnt == 15 {
                dll_rst = 0
                ss = 2
            }
        } else if ss == 2 {
            if s_dll == 1 {
                ss = 3
                scnt = 0
                dll_freeze = 1
            }
        } else if ss < 9 {
            // eight cycles a step
            if scnt == 7 {
                scnt = 0
                ss = ss + 1
                if ss == 3 { eclk_stop = 1 }
                if ss == 4 { ddr_rst = 1 }
                if ss == 5 { ddr_rst = 0 }
                if ss == 6 { eclk_stop = 0 }
                if ss == 7 { dll_freeze = 0 }
                if ss == 8 { init_pause = 1 }
            }
        } else if ss == 9 {
            // UDDCNTL_N low for cycles 3-10 of 16 with PAUSE
            if scnt == 3 { init_udd_n = 0 }
            if scnt == 11 { init_udd_n = 1 }
            if scnt == 15 {
                init_pause = 0
                ss = 10
                io_ready = 1
            }
        }
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ DLL code updates (SCLK)
    // each controller update window takes the DLL's code to the DQS buffers with their clocks
    // paused for 7 cycles, so a controller holds dfi_ctrlupd_req at least 8 cycles (the DFI
    // controller's CTRLUPD_CYC)
    signal upd_cnt: bit[4] = 0
    signal upd_pause: bit = 0
    signal upd_udd_n: bit = 1
    let dll_udd_n: bit = init_udd_n & upd_udd_n
    let io_pause: bit = init_pause | upd_pause

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ init (SCLK)
    // 0 wait for init start and the DDR reset sequence, 3 hold the lanes in reset,
    // 4 load the settings, 5 wait for the delays to move, 6 done
    #[cdc]
    signal io_ready_m: bit = 0
    signal io_ready_s: bit = 0
    signal ist: bit[3] = 0
    signal icnt: bit[16] = 0
    signal dqs_rst: bit = 1
    signal load: bit = 0
    signal init_done_r: bit = 0
    signal ctrlupd_ack_r: bit = 0
    signal ctrlupd_n: bit[16] = 0

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ DFI frames
    // c: captured (newest), b: being sent to the I/O logic, a and a2: older
    signal c_cs: bit[4] = 0
    signal c_ca: bit[24] = 0
    signal c_cke: bit[4] = 0
    signal c_rst: bit[4] = 0
    signal c_we: bit[4] = 0
    signal c_wd: bit[128] = 0
    signal c_re: bit[4] = 0
    signal c_wls: bit = 0
    signal b_cs: bit[4] = 0
    signal b_ca: bit[24] = 0
    signal b_cke: bit[4] = 0
    signal b_rst: bit[4] = 0
    signal b_we: bit[4] = 0
    signal b_wd: bit[128] = 0
    signal b_re: bit[4] = 0
    signal b_wls: bit = 0
    // the frames after a write leveling strobe's first
    signal b_wls1: bit = 0
    signal b_wls2: bit = 0
    signal a_we: bit[4] = 0
    signal a_wd: bit[128] = 0
    signal a_re: bit[4] = 0
    signal rst_n_r: bit = 0
    // training enables, as of frame b
    signal c_wl_en: bit = 0
    signal c_gate_en: bit = 0
    signal c_eye_en: bit = 0
    signal c_wdq_en: bit = 0
    signal b_wl_en: bit = 0
    signal b_gate_en: bit = 0
    signal b_eye_en: bit = 0
    signal b_wdq_en: bit = 0
    signal wdq_q: bit = 0
    // write slots captured, mod 8 (a beat's place in its burst, for the write DQ pattern)
    signal wcap: bit[3] = 0
    // per-lane DQ output enables (1 = not driven)
    signal dq_tt0: bit[4] = 15
    signal dq_tt1: bit[4] = 15

    let wde0: bit[3] = {2'b00, dfi_wrdata_en_p0}
    let wde1: bit[3] = {2'b00, dfi_wrdata_en_p1}
    let wde2: bit[3] = {2'b00, dfi_wrdata_en_p2}
    let wi1: bit[3] = wcap + wde0
    let wi2: bit[3] = wi1 + wde1
    let wi3: bit[3] = wi2 + wde2
    let wcap_next: bit[3] = wi3 + {2'b00, dfi_wrdata_en_p3}
    let wdp0: bit[32] = nx_wdq_word(wcap)
    let wdp1: bit[32] = nx_wdq_word(wi1)
    let wdp2: bit[32] = nx_wdq_word(wi2)
    let wdp3: bit[32] = nx_wdq_word(wi3)

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ frame b at the pins
    // slot k of the window {c, b, a}: k = 0..3 frame a, 4..7 frame b, 8..11 frame c
    let we12: bit[12] = {c_we, b_we, a_we}
    let wd12: bit[384] = {c_wd, b_wd, a_wd}
    // a slot with wrdata_en is sent in the next slot: e(j) = we12[3 + j] for frame b's slot j

    let e0: bit = we12[3]
    let e1: bit = we12[4]
    let e2: bit = we12[5]
    let e3: bit = we12[6]
    let em1: bit = we12[2]
    let e4: bit = we12[7]
    let e5: bit = we12[8]
    // DQS: 2 slots of preamble, the data slots, 1 slot of postamble; DQ: a slot of lead, the data
    // slots and one more holding the last beat
    let sdrv0: bit = if em1 == 1 || e0 == 1 || e1 == 1 || e2 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ws0: bit[32] = wd12[127:96]
    let wp0: bit[32] = wd12[95:64]
    let bt0_0: bit[16] = if e0 == 1 { ws0[15:0] } else { wp0[31:16] }
    let bt1_0: bit[16] = if e0 == 1 { ws0[31:16] } else { wp0[31:16] }
    let sdrv1: bit = if e0 == 1 || e1 == 1 || e2 == 1 || e3 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ws1: bit[32] = wd12[159:128]
    let wp1: bit[32] = wd12[127:96]
    let bt0_1: bit[16] = if e1 == 1 { ws1[15:0] } else { wp1[31:16] }
    let bt1_1: bit[16] = if e1 == 1 { ws1[31:16] } else { wp1[31:16] }
    let sdrv2: bit = if e1 == 1 || e2 == 1 || e3 == 1 || e4 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ws2: bit[32] = wd12[191:160]
    let wp2: bit[32] = wd12[159:128]
    let bt0_2: bit[16] = if e2 == 1 { ws2[15:0] } else { wp2[31:16] }
    let bt1_2: bit[16] = if e2 == 1 { ws2[31:16] } else { wp2[31:16] }
    let sdrv3: bit = if e2 == 1 || e3 == 1 || e4 == 1 || e5 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ws3: bit[32] = wd12[223:192]
    let wp3: bit[32] = wd12[191:160]
    let bt0_3: bit[16] = if e3 == 1 { ws3[15:0] } else { wp3[31:16] }
    let bt1_3: bit[16] = if e3 == 1 { ws3[31:16] } else { wp3[31:16] }
    let dqs_tt_w: bit[4] = {~sdrv3, ~sdrv2, ~sdrv1, ~sdrv0}
    // DQ output enables (1 = not driven): DQ drives in slot j when e(j + 1), e(j) or e(j - 1) is
    // set. The slot of lead (inside the DQS preamble, so no wider than the strobe's drive) turns
    // the drivers on before the first beat: without it a lone write's first beat reached the
    // DRAM undriven on silicon.
    // Registered from the frames they come from (b and c now are a and b next cycle), one
    // register per lane so each sits by its lane's gearboxes
    let nqdrv0: bit = if c_we[0] == 1 || b_we[3] == 1 || b_we[2] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let nqdrv1: bit = if c_we[1] == 1 || c_we[0] == 1 || b_we[3] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let nqdrv2: bit = if c_we[2] == 1 || c_we[1] == 1 || c_we[0] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let nqdrv3: bit = if c_we[3] == 1 || c_we[2] == 1 || c_we[1] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let dq_tt_next: bit[4] = {~nqdrv3, ~nqdrv2, ~nqdrv1, ~nqdrv0}
    // DQS rises at the start of each data slot. A write leveling strobe takes three frames: a
    // frame of preamble (driven low), four pulses (the DQS buffer returns a word per four
    // strobe pulses, so the feedback needs at least four) and a frame of postamble
    let dqs_d_w: bit[8] = {1'b0, e3, 1'b0, e2, 1'b0, e1, 1'b0, e0}
    let wl_any: bit = if b_wls == 1 || b_wls1 == 1 || b_wls2 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let dqs_d: bit[8] = if b_wls1 == 1 { 8'b01010101 } else { if wl_any == 1 { 8'b00000000 } else { dqs_d_w } }
    let dqs_tt: bit[4] = if wl_any == 1 { 4'b0000 } else { dqs_tt_w }
    // the read gate around a write strobe, as around a write leveling strobe: from the last
    // preamble slot to two slots past the last pulse (slot j: e(j + 1), e(j), e(j - 1), e(j - 2))
    let wg0: bit = if we12[4] == 1 || e0 == 1 || em1 == 1 || we12[1] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wg1: bit = if e2 == 1 || e1 == 1 || e0 == 1 || em1 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wg2: bit = if e3 == 1 || e2 == 1 || e1 == 1 || e0 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wg3: bit = if e4 == 1 || e3 == 1 || e2 == 1 || e1 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wr_gate: bit[4] = if wl_any == 1 { 4'b0000 } else { {wg3, wg2, wg1, wg0} }
    let dq_d0: bit[64] = {bt1_3[7], bt0_3[7], bt1_2[7], bt0_2[7], bt1_1[7], bt0_1[7], bt1_0[7], bt0_0[7], bt1_3[6], bt0_3[6], bt1_2[6], bt0_2[6], bt1_1[6], bt0_1[6], bt1_0[6], bt0_0[6], bt1_3[5], bt0_3[5], bt1_2[5], bt0_2[5], bt1_1[5], bt0_1[5], bt1_0[5], bt0_0[5], bt1_3[4], bt0_3[4], bt1_2[4], bt0_2[4], bt1_1[4], bt0_1[4], bt1_0[4], bt0_0[4], bt1_3[3], bt0_3[3], bt1_2[3], bt0_2[3], bt1_1[3], bt0_1[3], bt1_0[3], bt0_0[3], bt1_3[2], bt0_3[2], bt1_2[2], bt0_2[2], bt1_1[2], bt0_1[2], bt1_0[2], bt0_0[2], bt1_3[1], bt0_3[1], bt1_2[1], bt0_2[1], bt1_1[1], bt0_1[1], bt1_0[1], bt0_0[1], bt1_3[0], bt0_3[0], bt1_2[0], bt0_2[0], bt1_1[0], bt0_1[0], bt1_0[0], bt0_0[0]}
    let dq_d1: bit[64] = {bt1_3[15], bt0_3[15], bt1_2[15], bt0_2[15], bt1_1[15], bt0_1[15], bt1_0[15], bt0_0[15], bt1_3[14], bt0_3[14], bt1_2[14], bt0_2[14], bt1_1[14], bt0_1[14], bt1_0[14], bt0_0[14], bt1_3[13], bt0_3[13], bt1_2[13], bt0_2[13], bt1_1[13], bt0_1[13], bt1_0[13], bt0_0[13], bt1_3[12], bt0_3[12], bt1_2[12], bt0_2[12], bt1_1[12], bt0_1[12], bt1_0[12], bt0_0[12], bt1_3[11], bt0_3[11], bt1_2[11], bt0_2[11], bt1_1[11], bt0_1[11], bt1_0[11], bt0_0[11], bt1_3[10], bt0_3[10], bt1_2[10], bt0_2[10], bt1_1[10], bt0_1[10], bt1_0[10], bt0_0[10], bt1_3[9], bt0_3[9], bt1_2[9], bt0_2[9], bt1_1[9], bt0_1[9], bt1_0[9], bt0_0[9], bt1_3[8], bt0_3[8], bt1_2[8], bt0_2[8], bt1_1[8], bt0_1[8], bt1_0[8], bt0_0[8]}

    // read gate window: rddata_en of frames a, b, c (the gate opens two SCLK cycles after
    // READ, and the data comes back later than that, so the sweep starts from frame c)
    let rd_win: bit[12] = {c_re, b_re, a_re}
    let b_training: bit = if b_wl_en == 1 || b_gate_en == 1 || b_eye_en == 1 || b_wdq_en == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rd_burst: bit = if b_re != 0 && a_re == 0 && (b_gate_en == 1 || b_eye_en == 1 || b_wdq_en == 1) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let tr_start: bit = if (b_wl_en == 1 && b_wls == 1) || rd_burst == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let pat: bit[16] = RDC_PATTERN
    let inv0: bit[8] = RDC_INV0
    let inv1: bit[8] = RDC_INV1
    let exp_rdc0: bit[128] = nx_rdc_lane(pat, inv0)
    let exp_rdc1: bit[128] = nx_rdc_lane(pat, inv1)
    let exp_wdq0: bit[128] = nx_wdq_lane(0)
    let exp_wdq1: bit[128] = ~nx_wdq_lane(0)

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ command pins
    inst ck_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: 0, D1: 1, D2: 0, D3: 1, D4: 0, D5: 1, D6: 0, D7: 1,
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ckc_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: 1, D1: 0, D2: 1, D3: 0, D4: 1, D5: 0, D6: 1, D7: 0,
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca0_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_ca[0], D1: b_ca[0], D2: b_ca[6], D3: b_ca[6], D4: b_ca[12], D5: b_ca[12], D6: b_ca[18], D7: b_ca[18],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca0_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: ca0_od.Q }
    inst ca1_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_ca[1], D1: b_ca[1], D2: b_ca[7], D3: b_ca[7], D4: b_ca[13], D5: b_ca[13], D6: b_ca[19], D7: b_ca[19],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca1_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: ca1_od.Q }
    inst ca2_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_ca[2], D1: b_ca[2], D2: b_ca[8], D3: b_ca[8], D4: b_ca[14], D5: b_ca[14], D6: b_ca[20], D7: b_ca[20],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca2_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: ca2_od.Q }
    inst ca3_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_ca[3], D1: b_ca[3], D2: b_ca[9], D3: b_ca[9], D4: b_ca[15], D5: b_ca[15], D6: b_ca[21], D7: b_ca[21],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca3_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: ca3_od.Q }
    inst ca4_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_ca[4], D1: b_ca[4], D2: b_ca[10], D3: b_ca[10], D4: b_ca[16], D5: b_ca[16], D6: b_ca[22], D7: b_ca[22],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca4_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: ca4_od.Q }
    inst ca5_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_ca[5], D1: b_ca[5], D2: b_ca[11], D3: b_ca[11], D4: b_ca[17], D5: b_ca[17], D6: b_ca[23], D7: b_ca[23],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst ca5_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: ca5_od.Q }
    inst cke_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_cke[0], D1: b_cke[0], D2: b_cke[1], D3: b_cke[1], D4: b_cke[2], D5: b_cke[2], D6: b_cke[3], D7: b_cke[3],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst cke_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: cke_od.Q }
    inst cs_od = ODDRX4 {
        D0: b_cs[0], D1: b_cs[0], D2: b_cs[1], D3: b_cs[1], D4: b_cs[2], D5: b_cs[2], D6: b_cs[3], D7: b_cs[3],
        ECLK: eclk_ca, SCLK: sclk, RST: ddr_rst
    }
    inst cs_dl = DELAYB<CA_DELAY> { A: cs_od.Q }

    inst lane0 = NexusLpddr4Lane<DQ_IN_DELAY, GATE_SLOTS, TRAIN_WIN, WL_STEP, WL_MAX, EYE_STEP, EYE_HALF, WDQ_STEP, WDQ_HALF> {
        eclk: eclk_dq, sclk: sclk, rst: dqs_rst, io_rst: ddr_rst, io_pause: io_pause,
        load: load, dllcode: dll.CODE,
        dq_d: dq_d0, dq_tt: dq_tt0, dqs_d: dqs_d, dqs_tt: dqs_tt, rd_win: rd_win,
        wl_frame: {b_wls2, b_wls1, b_wls}, wr_gate: wr_gate, tr_start: tr_start,
        wl_en: b_wl_en, gate_en: b_gate_en, eye_en: b_eye_en, wdq_en: b_wdq_en,
        exp_rdc: exp_rdc0, exp_wdq: exp_wdq0,
        dq_i: dq_i[7:0], dqs_i: dqs_i[0]
    }

    inst lane1 = NexusLpddr4Lane<DQ_IN_DELAY, GATE_SLOTS, TRAIN_WIN, WL_STEP, WL_MAX, EYE_STEP, EYE_HALF, WDQ_STEP, WDQ_HALF> {
        eclk: eclk_dq, sclk: sclk, rst: dqs_rst, io_rst: ddr_rst, io_pause: io_pause,
        load: load, dllcode: dll.CODE,
        dq_d: dq_d1, dq_tt: dq_tt1, dqs_d: dqs_d, dqs_tt: dqs_tt, rd_win: rd_win,
        wl_frame: {b_wls2, b_wls1, b_wls}, wr_gate: wr_gate, tr_start: tr_start,
        wl_en: b_wl_en, gate_en: b_gate_en, eye_en: b_eye_en, wdq_en: b_wdq_en,
        exp_rdc: exp_rdc1, exp_wdq: exp_wdq1,
        dq_i: dq_i[15:8], dqs_i: dqs_i[1]
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ read data out
    signal q0: [bit[64]; 4]
    signal q1: [bit[64]; 4]
    signal qw0: bit[2] = 0
    signal qw1: bit[2] = 0
    signal qr: bit[2] = 0
    signal qn0: bit[3] = 0
    signal qn1: bit[3] = 0
    signal rdw0: bit[32] = 0
    signal rdw1: bit[32] = 0
    signal rdw2: bit[32] = 0
    signal rdw3: bit[32] = 0
    signal rdv: bit = 0
    let have: bit = if qn0 != 0 && qn1 != 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let oa0: bit[64] = q0[qr]
    let oa1: bit[64] = q1[qr]
    // the PLL and DLL lock flags change with no relation to SCLK: two registers each
    #[cdc]
    signal pll_lock_m: bit = 0
    signal pll_lock_s: bit = 0
    #[cdc]
    signal dll_lock_m: bit = 0
    signal dll_lock_s: bit = 0
    let push0: bit = lane0.dv
    let push1: bit = lane1.dv

    on(sclk.rise) {
        pll_lock_m = pll_lock
        pll_lock_s = pll_lock_m
        dll_lock_m = dll.LOCK
        dll_lock_s = dll_lock_m
        io_ready_m = io_ready
        io_ready_s = io_ready_m
        // ---------------------------------------------------------- init
        if ist == 0 {
            dqs_rst = 1
            if dfi_init_start == 1 && io_ready_s == 1 {
                ist = 3
                icnt = 0
            }
        } else if ist == 3 {
            icnt = icnt + 1
            if icnt == 7 {
                dqs_rst = 0
                ist = 4
                icnt = 0
            }
        } else if ist == 4 {
            load = 1
            icnt = icnt + 1
            if icnt == 3 {
                load = 0
                ist = 5
                icnt = 0
            }
        } else if ist == 5 {
            icnt = icnt + 1
            if icnt > 4 && lane0.busy == 0 && lane1.busy == 0 {
                ist = 6
                init_done_r = 1
            }
        }
        if dfi_ctrlupd_req == 1 && ctrlupd_ack_r == 0 {
            ctrlupd_n = ctrlupd_n + 1
            upd_cnt = 1
        } else if upd_cnt != 0 {
            upd_cnt = if upd_cnt == 7 { 0 } else { upd_cnt + 1 }
        }
        // PAUSE through cycles 1-7 of the window, UDDCNTL_N low in 3-5
        upd_pause = if upd_cnt != 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
        upd_udd_n = if upd_cnt >= 3 && upd_cnt < 6 { 0 } else { 1 }
        ctrlupd_ack_r = dfi_ctrlupd_req

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- frames
        c_cs = {dfi_cs_p3, dfi_cs_p2, dfi_cs_p1, dfi_cs_p0}
        c_ca = {dfi_address_p3, dfi_address_p2, dfi_address_p1, dfi_address_p0}
        c_cke = {dfi_cke_p3, dfi_cke_p2, dfi_cke_p1, dfi_cke_p0}
        c_rst = {dfi_reset_n_p3, dfi_reset_n_p2, dfi_reset_n_p1, dfi_reset_n_p0}
        c_we = {dfi_wrdata_en_p3, dfi_wrdata_en_p2, dfi_wrdata_en_p1, dfi_wrdata_en_p0}
        // write DQ training: the PHY's own data in place of the controller's
        c_wd = if dfi_wdqlvl_en == 1 { {wdp3, wdp2, wdp1, wdp0} } else { {dfi_wrdata_p3, dfi_wrdata_p2, dfi_wrdata_p1, dfi_wrdata_p0} }
        wcap = if dfi_wdqlvl_en == 1 && wdq_q == 0 { 3'b000 } else { wcap_next }
        wdq_q = dfi_wdqlvl_en
        c_re = {dfi_rddata_en_p3, dfi_rddata_en_p2, dfi_rddata_en_p1, dfi_rddata_en_p0}
        c_wls = if dfi_wrlvl_en == 1 && dfi_wrlvl_strobe == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
        c_wl_en = dfi_wrlvl_en
        c_gate_en = dfi_rdlvl_gate_en
        c_eye_en = dfi_rdlvl_en
        c_wdq_en = dfi_wdqlvl_en
        b_cs = c_cs
        b_ca = c_ca
        b_cke = c_cke
        b_rst = c_rst
        b_we = c_we
        b_wd = c_wd
        b_re = c_re
        b_wls2 = b_wls1
        b_wls1 = b_wls
        b_wls = c_wls
        b_wl_en = c_wl_en
        b_gate_en = c_gate_en
        b_eye_en = c_eye_en
        b_wdq_en = c_wdq_en
        a_we = b_we
        dq_tt0 = dq_tt_next
        dq_tt1 = dq_tt_next
        a_wd = b_wd
        a_re = b_re
        rst_n_r = b_rst[0]

        // ---------------------------------------------------------- read data
        if push0 == 1 {
            q0[qw0] = lane0.half
            qw0 = qw0 + 1
        }
        if push1 == 1 {
            q1[qw1] = lane1.half
            qw1 = qw1 + 1
        }
        if have == 1 {
            qr = qr + 1
            rdw0 = {oa1[15:8], oa0[15:8], oa1[7:0], oa0[7:0]}
            rdw1 = {oa1[31:24], oa0[31:24], oa1[23:16], oa0[23:16]}
            rdw2 = {oa1[47:40], oa0[47:40], oa1[39:32], oa0[39:32]}
            rdw3 = {oa1[63:56], oa0[63:56], oa1[55:48], oa0[55:48]}
        }
        rdv = have
        qn0 = if push0 == 1 && have == 0 { qn0 + 1 } else { if push0 == 0 && have == 1 { qn0 - 1 } else { qn0 } }
        qn1 = if push1 == 1 && have == 0 { qn1 + 1 } else { if push1 == 0 && have == 1 { qn1 - 1 } else { qn1 } }
    }

    dfi_clk = sclk
    dfi_rddata_w0 = rdw0
    dfi_rddata_w1 = rdw1
    dfi_rddata_w2 = rdw2
    dfi_rddata_w3 = rdw3
    dfi_rddata_valid_w0 = rdv
    dfi_rddata_valid_w1 = rdv
    dfi_rddata_valid_w2 = rdv
    dfi_rddata_valid_w3 = rdv
    dfi_init_complete = init_done_r
    dfi_ctrlupd_ack = ctrlupd_ack_r
    dfi_phyupd_req = 0
    dfi_rdlvl_gate_resp = {lane1.resp_gate, lane0.resp_gate}
    dfi_rdlvl_resp = {lane1.resp_eye, lane0.resp_eye}
    dfi_wrlvl_resp = {lane1.resp_wl, lane0.resp_wl}
    dfi_wdqlvl_resp = {lane1.resp_wdq, lane0.resp_wdq}

    ck_t = ck_od.Q
    ck_c = ckc_od.Q
    cke = cke_dl.Z
    cs = cs_dl.Z
    ca = {ca5_dl.Z, ca4_dl.Z, ca3_dl.Z, ca2_dl.Z, ca1_dl.Z, ca0_dl.Z}
    reset_n = rst_n_r
    dq_o = {lane1.dq_o, lane0.dq_o}
    dq_t = {lane1.dq_t, lane0.dq_t}
    dqs_o = {lane1.dqs_o, lane0.dqs_o}
    dqs_t = {lane1.dqs_t, lane0.dqs_t}
    dqs_c_o = {lane1.dqs_c_o, lane0.dqs_c_o}
    dqs_c_t = {lane1.dqs_c_t, lane0.dqs_c_t}
    dmi_o = {lane1.dmi_o, lane0.dmi_o}
    dmi_t = {lane1.dmi_t, lane0.dmi_t}

    dll_lock = dll_lock_s
    gate_dly0 = lane0.gate_set
    gate_dly1 = lane1.gate_set
    rd_dly0 = lane0.rd_pos
    rd_dly1 = lane1.rd_pos
    wl_dly0 = lane0.wl_pos
    wl_dly1 = lane1.wl_pos
    wdq_dly0 = lane0.wr_pos
    wdq_dly1 = lane1.wr_pos
    gate_fail = {lane1.gate_fail, lane0.gate_fail}
    lvl_fail = {lane1.eye_fail, lane0.eye_fail}
    wrlvl_fail = {lane1.wl_fail, lane0.wl_fail}
    wdq_fail = {lane1.wdq_fail, lane0.wdq_fail}
    bursts0 = lane0.bursts
    bursts1 = lane1.bursts
    sweep_map0 = lane0.sweep_map
    rd_lat0 = lane0.rd_lat_o
    rd_lat1 = lane1.rd_lat_o
    sweep_map1 = lane1.sweep_map
    ctrlupd_count = ctrlupd_n
}
